# Oracle + legacy boundaries
- Inspect version, driver compatibility, synonyms, packages, grants, triggers and schema ownership before designing access.
- Legacy database and applications must coexist until explicit cutover. Do not change their behavior accidentally.
- Every proposed database change requires documented dependencies, impact assessment, backup/rollback plan and separate written approval.
- Full hourly snapshots MUST be preserved, including unchanged wagons; changes-file data is a separate flow. Never collapse snapshots to delta-only history.
- For import design: source-file identity, batch IDs, deduplication policy, atomicity/restart behavior and reconciliation must be explicit.
- Document all old-app ↔ new-app parity checks with representative test cases and concrete evidence.
